# c2: gnss-ssv
# c3: lunar-infrastructure
# c4: holdover-test
seg-d0b2811a3d3c = The engine has { "92" } scenario kinds; <c1/> lists them with their fields. New in { "0.38.0" }: <c2/> (GNSS signals for spacecraft above, around and past the GNSS orbits) and <c3/> (lunar orbit and surface as navigation and geodetic infrastructure), both MODELLED, and <c4/> (a time-error record against the ITU-T masks).

# text
seg-68ed88ec0b32 = <b>Spectrum</b>: how a jammer takes the GNSS L band, band by band.

# text
seg-f04a0aeeee33 = <b>Clocks and timing</b>: holdover against a threshold, time transfer, and telecom holdover against the masks of the International Telecommunication Union's standardization sector (ITU-T).

# text
seg-7e38ac603ef2 = <b>Constellations around any body</b>: coverage, dilution of precision and availability around the Earth, the Moon or Mars, and the solar system at one epoch.

# text
seg-82708b06dcc6 = <b>Low-Earth-orbit navigation</b>: signal, pass and link, navigation message, and a fused fix, stage by stage.

# text
seg-e21e9bb02d00 = <b>Campaigns</b>: a chained mission, a sweep or a Monte Carlo ensemble in one scenario.

# text
seg-ba5057da54e4 = <b>Reports, animation and exports</b>: every figure with its unit and label; an animated drawing of a run; SP3 (Standard Product { "3" }), CCSDS (Consultative Committee for Space Data Systems) orbit messages, CZML (Cesium Language), KML (Keyhole Markup Language), GeoJSON, STK (Systems Tool Kit) and SigMF (Signal Metadata Format) files.

# attr:alt
seg-6b43a8c3031e = One open engine at the centre, kshana { $version }, with a typed dispatch over { "75" } kinds; around it the command line, the Rust library, Python, WebAssembly and Kshana Studio, the MCP server, the Docker image and the JetBrains plugin; below it Kshana Pro, a proprietary overlay that depends on the open engine and never forks it

# text
# c1: kshana-mcp
seg-ea6f46d62e7b = The same scenario file gives the same bytes on every surface. MCP is the Model Context Protocol: <a1><c1/></a1> lets an AI (artificial intelligence) assistant run the engine.

# text
seg-f51b0a8cd30e = Six papers on arXiv are built on the open engine, each with the command behind it: <a1>arXiv:{ "2606.22054" }</a1> (the optimism gap of interference detectors), <a2>arXiv:{ "2606.24210" }</a2> (a conditional timing protection level), <a3>arXiv:{ "2607.05415" }</a3> (how stable a PNT resilience score is), <a4>arXiv:{ "2607.02566" }</a4> (lunar surface station observability with very-long-baseline interferometry), <a5>arXiv:{ "2607.06212" }</a5> (lunar south-polar geometry and surface beacons) and <a6>arXiv:{ "2610.23871" }</a6> (cislunar navigation as an observability problem: arc length, Gramian conditioning and the Doppler lever). See <a7>Research</a7>.

